            <ArticleTitle>Hand burn management: minimising pain and trauma at dressing change.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S46, S48-50</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The aim of wound management in hand burn injuries is to restore function and prevent problem scars, so a key consideration in wound healing is the removal of dressings without causing pain and further trauma as well as preserving function. Conventionally, wound dressings such as paraffin gauze were used for burn injuries, but this led to pain and trauma on removal, as well as drying out. This study looks at the use of Mepitel® One on hand burns; this dressing incorporates all the benefits of Mepitel, however, it only has Safetac technology on the wound contact side, allowing easy handling and application.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
